/P 157 0 R
/E (It symbolizes the "dignity of labor." For the Rivera-Quiapo family, it is a testament to the socioeconomic mobility of their ancestors. It represents the era before the mechanization of agriculture, where the relationship between the farmer, the carabao, and the hand-carved plow was the foundation of the community's survival.)
