/T (The object demonstrates clear provenance, originating from local communities where wood carpentry was an a very essential skill as houses before are mainly made out of wood materials; it is representative of craftsmanship and carpentry that was practiced by the locals; its continued rarity is absolute since it is one of the few tools that was carefully preserved to this day; and it has high interpretative potential, offering insight to traditional carpentry methods.)
